# Git-Hooks sind reine lokale Tooling-Konfiguration (Allowlist-Guard,
# gitleaks, Changelog-Gate) -- laufen nur auf der eigenen Maschine über
# core.hooksPath, gehören nicht ins öffentliche Repo.
.githooks/
# Alle internen Tools (Promo-Pipeline, Changelog-Gate) laufen ausschließlich
# lokal, nie auf GitHub.
tools/

# OSS-Allowlist-Policy selbst: rein lokale Enforcement-Konfiguration, hat auf
# GitHub nichts verloren (Compliance-Cleanup 2026-08-14) — .githooks/pre-commit
# und pre-push laufen fail-open (WARN statt Block), wenn die Datei fehlt.
.ossallowlist

# Repo-level Dev-Tooling (Node-Skripte ohne Public-Bezug: Brand-Name-Linter,
# Allowlist-Hash-Helper, Shortcuts-Doku-Generator, Driver-Install-Skript) --
# nie public, Compliance-Cleanup 2026-08-14.
/scripts/

# Secrets
.env
.env.local

# Node / pnpm workspace
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
.astro/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# apps/extension ships its own .vscode/launch.json + tasks.json (F5 debug
# launch for the extension itself, same convention as the PoC it replaced) —
# un-ignore just that one directory from the blanket .vscode/ rule above.
!apps/extension/.vscode/
!apps/extension/.vscode/*.json

# apps/extension build/test artifacts — vsix packaging temp files, compiled
# test output, and the @vscode/test-electron download cache.
apps/extension/*.vsix
apps/extension/out-test/
apps/extension/.vscode-test/

# Internal HyperFrames promo-video authoring project — AGENTS.md/BRIEF.md/
# assets/hyperframes.json are the internal tool's own scaffolding, never a
# public deliverable (2026-09-09: was mistakenly allowlisted and pushed
# publicly, then untracked/gitignored again; see .ossallowlist's hard-deny
# note for the mechanism that now prevents this recurring). The finished
# public output lives separately at apps/website/public/videos/, untouched.
videos/panecrew-promo/
